PATCH 538: FUN_0000_0ea9, the 3-lane proximity/range test, modelled each 32-bit coordinate lane as a
64-bit value -- and never set the carry its callers branch on.

This is the primitive under EVERY collision and proximity walk in the engine (bb1b, bb64, a0ab, 08e8,
...).  asm 0x0ea9-0x0f2f, DS=DGROUP=0x1c00, cx = the bound, bx/si = two coordinate triples:

     ea9: mov    %cx,%bp            ; bp = bound
     eab: xor    %cl,%cl            ; cl = sign flag
     ead: mov    (%bx),%ax          ; lane X low
     eaf: mov    0x2(%bx),%dx       ; lane X high   -> ONE int32, held as two words
     eb2: sub    (%si),%ax
     eb4: sbb    0x2(%si),%dx
     eb7: jns    0xec2
     eb9: dec    %cl               ; negative
     ebb: neg    %ax
     ebd: jae    0xf25             ; CF=0 only when ax was 0 -> neg dx
     ebf: xor    $0xffff,%dx       ; else 32-bit negate = neg ax / not dx
     ec2: jne    0xf23             ; high word != 0 -> FAIL (clc)
     ec4: cmp    %bp,%ax
     ec6: ja     0xf23             ; |delta| > bound (UNSIGNED) -> FAIL
     ec8: mov    %ax,0x2024        ; record lane X
     ecb: mov    %dx,0x2026
     ecf: mov    %cl,0x2030        ; BYTE
     ed3: xor    %cl,%cl
     ed5: mov    0x4(%bx),%ax      ; lane Y at +4/+6 ... same shape, records 0x2028/0x202a/0x2031
     eff: mov    0x8(%bx),%ax      ; lane Z at +8/+0xa
     f0b: mov    %ax,0x202c        ; recorded BEFORE the abs -- the SIGNED delta
     f0e: mov    %dx,0x202e
     f12: jns    0xf1d             ; ... and NO bound check: the test is 2-D by design
     f1d: mov    %cl,0x2032        ; BYTE
     f21: stc                      ; HIT
     f22: ret
     f23: clc                      ; MISS
     f24: ret

Two defects, both fatal to combat:

1. WIDTH/LANE.  Ghidra typed the operands `uint *` and paired element[0] (=X) with element[1] (=Y) as
   one lane's low and high halves.  So lane 1 compared X against a "high word" that is really Y, lane 2
   compared Z, and Y was never compared at all.  Its `uVar5 ^ 0xffff` also flips only the low 16 bits
   of a 32-bit variable, so the negate is not the asm's `neg ax` / `xor dx,0xffff` pair either.

2. NO CARRY.  The pristine function never assigns g_fist_cf, yet every caller branches on it -- bb1b
   is `call 0ea9; jae <next candidate>` (patch 284 threads the carry through g_fist_cf).  The range
   test's answer was therefore a STALE carry left behind by an unrelated call.

Measured in AZER1 self-play before this patch: all 8000 sampled projectile range tests "hit", and 7994
of those hits were against the six type-0x1b objects -- which sit at z=7936..13824 while the vehicles
sit at z=1280..2048.  Each bogus hit ran the impact path and spawned a type-0x4 explosion template, so
the small-object roster (a294, cap 0x96=150 in b21d) saturated and refused 7429 further allocations;
with the roster full no unit could fire a projectile at all.

After: a294 150 -> 114 (no longer saturating), a296 11 -> 16 (the spurious kills are gone), and the
simulation runs materially further (op-0x58 LOS queries 17795 -> 30190 over the same tick budget).

Lane Z stays deliberately un-gated, exactly as the asm has it.  The 0x2030/0x2031/0x2032 stores are
BYTE stores; the DAT_1000_e030/e031 macros are undefined2 and would clobber the neighbouring lane's
sign byte, so this writes bytes.

